# ReXGlue SDK changes for WWE 2K14 (session63-64-android): c33dc62ba917..61ca96d9f003 on wwe2k14-local
# Apply in order on upstream rexglue/rexglue-sdk f5337cd (git apply). Commits (first parent):
#  61ca96d wwe2k14 Android port, step 9: AllocFixed's commit on a reserved range checks the range with msync(MS_ASYNC) instead of parsing /proc/self/maps (Android, Session 64)
#  b773aab wwe2k14 Android port, step 8: no spinning waits, no /proc/self/maps per watch fault (Session 64)
#  c7444eb wwe2k14 Android port, step 7: an on-disk VkPipelineCache (vulkan_disk_pipeline_cache, default on on Android only): <cache>/shaders/shareable/TITLE.vkpc for the emulated path's and NATIVE's per-shader pipelines, loaded with the shader storage, saved in the background after new pipelines. Phone attract demo: load to the match clock 15.4 s cold -> 9.7 s warm, worst frame after the bell 147 -> 85 ms (runs 022 / 023)
#  a1f55c5 wwe2k14 Android port, step 6: drain the async submit queue before a fence wait on Android (Adreno never wakes a wait on a fence vkQueueSubmit has not received). Played match 39.7 -> 47.7 fps mean with vulkan_async_submit (runs 017 / 020)
#  e4b27a3 wwe2k14 Android port, step 5: fence waits in 1 s steps on Android (Adreno returns VK_TIMEOUT from an infinite wait), the fence wait's VkResult in its error line
#  8204a6d wwe2k14 Android port, step 4: thread fibers work on Android (the runtime converts every guest thread; only Create / SwitchTo abort); logs\ and the config file in the app's files folder (the install folder is read-only). Phone run 004: title screen
#  e340229 wwe2k14 Android port, step 3: one app per library on Android too (no XE_UI_WINDOWED_APPS_IN_LIBRARY), so REX_DEFINE_APP gives the GetWindowedAppCreator SDL_main calls
#  d9da725 wwe2k14 Android port, step 2: SDL_main entry (WWE2K14_FILES_DIR as working folder + HOME, Android system init), GetExecutablePath = librexruntime.so (native library folder, GPU plugin next to it), logcat sink (tag wwe2k14) kept for the whole run
#  01306e2 wwe2k14 Android port, step 1: the SDK builds for arm64-v8a (NDK r29, API 28)

